  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the statement &quot;The match will be played only if the weather is good and ground is not wet&quot;. Select the correct negation from the following:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "09IAa",
      "text": "The match will not be played and weather is not good and ground is wet.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3JaFF",
      "text": "If the match will not be played, then either weather is not good or ground is wet.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8fKqI",
      "text": "The match will be played and weather is not good or ground is wet.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "mrbU3",
      "text": "The match will not be played or weather is good and ground is not wet.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>:</mo></math> weather is good<br />and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mo>:</mo></math> ground is not wet</p><p>Given&nbsp;statement &quot;The match will be played only if the weather is good and ground is not wet&quot; can be written as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, negation of&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>~</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></math></p><p>which is equivalent to &quot;The match will be played and weather is not good or ground is wet&quot;.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
